# Operis ERP — automated test suite environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env.test` and point it at a THROWAWAY local database only. The
# suite writes permanent rows (audit_log and the stock ledger are append-only
# by design — see docs/TESTING.md) and runs hundreds of multi-statement
# transactions, so it must never point at the database you demo or develop
# against (.env) and never at a shared/remote one by default.
#
# One-time setup (docs/TESTING.md):
#   1. Copy-Item .env.test.example .env.test
#   2. npm run test:db:up        (starts postgres:16 in Docker on port 54329)
#   3. npm run test:db:setup     (creates roles, database, migrates, grants, seeds currencies)
#   4. npm test

# --- Database ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Same two-role split as .env.example (mops_migrator / mops_runtime), pointed
# at the throwaway Docker Postgres from docker-compose.test.yml instead of
# your dev/demo database. scripts/test-db-setup.mjs creates these roles with
# these exact passwords if they don't already exist — change the passwords
# here AND re-run `npm run test:db:setup` if you ever change them.
MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://mops_migrator:test-migrator-password@localhost:54329/operis_test?schema=public"
RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://mops_runtime:test-runtime-password@localhost:54329/operis_test?schema=public"

# Superuser of the throwaway test server. Only scripts/test-db-setup.mjs uses
# this (to create the two roles above and the database itself, and to apply
# the Stage 3 runtime grants) — the application and the test suite itself
# never read this variable. Matches docker-compose.test.yml's POSTGRES_PASSWORD.
TEST_DB_ADMIN_URL="postgresql://postgres:devpassword@localhost:54329/postgres"

NODE_ENV=test

# --- Remote test database opt-in (vitest.test-env.ts) ------------------------
# Leave this unset. The suite refuses any non-local MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL /
# RUNTIME_DATABASE_URL by default — see docs/TESTING.md "Why not Neon" for the
# measured reasons (70-95 minute runs from connection-timeout retries, and the
# suite's permanent rows piling up in a database you don't control).
#
# If your team genuinely needs to run against a shared/branched remote
# database (e.g. a disposable Neon branch in CI), set ALL THREE of:
#   ALLOW_REMOTE_TEST_DB=1
#   TEST_DB_CONFIRM_TARGET=<database>@<host>   # copy the exact value from the
#                                               # error message vitest prints
#                                               # on first refusal — never type
#                                               # it from memory
# A target whose name matches /prod|production|live/ is refused even with
# both of the above set — see src/server/dev/test-db-guard.ts.
# ALLOW_REMOTE_TEST_DB=1
# TEST_DB_CONFIRM_TARGET=

# --- Timeouts (vitest.config.ts) ---------------------------------------------
# Defaults (30s / 60s) are sized for a local Docker Postgres. Raise both if you
# ever point this at a remote database (see "Why not Neon" above for why that's
# discouraged by default regardless).
# TEST_TIMEOUT_MS=30000
# TEST_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS=60000
